Example experimental patch (id 0): inserts a no-op marker comment into
version.h. It changes no behavior and exists only to exercise the
experimental-patches pipeline end to end.

Authored against RocksDB v11.8.1. Applied with `patch -p1 -F0`, so if a
context line drifts in another version it fails loudly rather than
fuzzing into the wrong place — build with `rocksdb_version: 11.8.1` to try it.

--- a/include/rocksdb/version.h
+++ b/include/rocksdb/version.h
@@ -5,3 +5,6 @@
 #pragma once
+// rocksdb-prebuilds experimental example patch (id 0): no-op marker demonstrating
+// the experimental-patches pipeline. Builds identically to stock RocksDB.
+//

 #include <string>
